# Cloudflare DNS Setup Guide

## If you are using your own server, refer to the following Nginx configuration to reverse proxy requests from your domain to geelark.com

```
server {
    listen 80;[cloudflare添加dns.md](cloudflare%E6%B7%BB%E5%8A%A0dns.md)
    server_name phone.test.com;
[cloudflare添加dns.md](cloudflare%E6%B7%BB%E5%8A%A0dns.md)

    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

[cloudflare添加dns.md](cloudflare%E6%B7%BB%E5%8A%A0dns.md)
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name phone.test.com;


    ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/test_com.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/test_com.key;


    location / {
        proxy_pass https://phone.geelark.com;
        proxy_ssl_server_name on;
        proxy_set_header Host phone.geelark.com;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}
```

## If you are using Cloudflare, follow the steps below

### 1. Add a Domain

Log in to Cloudflare, click "Domains" -> "Overview", then click "Add domain" in the top right corner. On the resulting page, select "Connect a domain".
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=9fca640af4f9c9e636d8648e45c98e61)
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=8873ae3259e6ec0e586ce6ded2c76182)

Enter your domain on the page and click "Continue", then select a plan. The page will display the DNS server addresses you need to change to.
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=1dfb950d2f7dcbb3bc64b6afe360a0cf)

Go to your domain registrar and change the DNS server addresses to the ones provided by Cloudflare.

### 2. Create a Worker

Go back to the Cloudflare dashboard, select "Worker Routes", and click "Manage Workers". On the new page, click "Create application". On the resulting page, click "Start with Hello World", enter a Worker name, and click "Deploy".
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=f8a70202ff1adec15017f9bc6ba6c5a8)
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=f7a7431bdb2ae3ba558035502d5b8834)
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=780ef62bed9b901885bf050c8a3055ac)
![](http://showdoc.geelark.com/server/index.php?s=/api/attachment/visitFile&sign=a22eae11b28561bfdb16833846c5baea)

### 3. Modify the Worker Code

Go to "Compute" -> "Workers & Pages", select the Worker you just deployed (in this example: phone-proxy), then click "Edit code" to modify the JS code.

Worker code (paste it in "Edit code"):

```js
/**
 * Welcome to Cloudflare Workers! This is your first worker.
 *
 * - Run "npm run dev" in your terminal to start a development server
 * - Open a browser tab at http://localhost:8787/ to see your worker in action
 * - Run "npm run deploy" to publish your worker
 *
 * Learn more at https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/
 */

export default {
  async fetch(request) {
    const url = new URL(request.url);

    url.hostname = "phone.geelark.com";

    const headers = new Headers(request.headers);

    // proxy_set_header Host phone.geelark.com;
    headers.set("Host", "phone.geelark.com");

    // proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    const clientIP = request.headers.get("CF-Connecting-IP");
    if (clientIP) {
      headers.set("X-Real-IP", clientIP);
      headers.set("X-Forwarded-For", clientIP);
    }

    // proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    headers.set("X-Forwarded-Proto", "https");

    const newRequest = new Request(url, {
      method: request.method,
      headers,
      body: request.method === "GET" || request.method === "HEAD"
        ? undefined
        : request.body,
      redirect: "follow",
    });

    return fetch(newRequest);
  },
};
```

